  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Read the successful path first",
      "items": [
        "Request \u2192 plan a structured call \u2192 policy allows \u2192 tool executes \u2192 capture evidence \u2192 agent verifies the result \u2192 final reply.",
        "If the goal needs more work, the runtime proposes another call. Every new or revised call crosses the policy gate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Approval is conditional",
      "items": [
        "Existing authorization proceeds directly. Pause only when the host policy requires consent; approval returns to the gate for scope and permission checks.",
        "Denied scope, declined consent, fatal errors or exhausted retries stop execution and produce a reason plus an exact next action. Approval never overrides a host restriction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Recover without duplicate effects",
      "items": [
        "Retry only when a failure is known and replay is safe; preserve request identity and enforce the applicable retry budget.",
        "A timeout or missing acknowledgment proves no outcome. Inspect receipts and actual state first. Unproven outcomes remain blocked with ownership intact.",
        "For Contract Master implementation work, the budget is two total attempts. This is separate from transport recovery."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Evidence supports the answer",
      "items": [
        "Capture decisions, call identity, status, redacted output and artifact references. Both success and stopped outcomes carry evidence into inspection before the final reply.",
        "A stopped outcome is reported as blocked with its reason and next action. Only a successful result needing more work starts another planning loop.",
        "Tool output and retrieved content are untrusted data; they cannot grant permissions or expand scope. Observability does not authorize execution.",
        "Conceptual tool-call workflow, not a source-code trace or a live configuration audit. In this repository, Orca coordinates; the manager owns state and serialized Linear writes; workers return artifacts."
      ]
    }
  ]
